#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100680 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20824866-0419-512a-b241-e3eb66b30194" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Function Given Some Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "6c57cb4e-244d-5058-91ef-9f74b15f2d35" :question/math-academy-id "e-7115" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(-1)=-1, f'(-1)=3, f''(-1)=-6$ and $f'''(-1)=6$. What is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=-1$?" :question/worked-solution "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_{3}(x) &= f(-1) + f^{′}(-1)(x + 1) + (f^{″}(-1))/(2!)(x + 1)^{2} + (f^{‴}(-1))/(3!)(x + 1)^{3} \\\\\n&= f(-1) + f^{′}(-1)(x + 1) + (f^{″}(-1))/(2)(x + 1)^{2} + (f^{‴}(-1))/(6)(x + 1)^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-1) &= -1 \\\\\nf^{′}(-1) &= 3 \\\\\nf^{″}(-1) &= -6 \\\\\nf^{‴}(-1) &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_{3}(x) &= -1 + 3(x + 1) + ((-6))/(2)(x + 1)^{2} + \\frac{6}{6}(x + 1)^{3} \\\\\n&=-1 + 3(x + 1) - 3(x + 1)^{2} + (x + 1)^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100691 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "66991fe4-9891-5308-87cf-cd38a3bad4a4" :question/math-academy-id "e-741" :question/problem "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = \\ln(1+x)$ about $x=0$." :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0$, we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\nP_3(x) = f(0) + f'(0)(x-0) + \\dfrac{1}{2!}f''(0)(x-0)^2 + \\dfrac{1}{3!}f'''(0)(x-0)^3\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0)$, $f'(0)$, $f''(0)$, and $f'''(0)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}f(x) &= \\ln (1 + x) & ⟹ & f(0)|= \\ln (1 + 0) = 0 \\\\ f^{′}(x)|= (1 + x)^{-1} & ⟹ & f^{′}(0)|= (1 + 0)^{-1} = 1 \\\\ f^{″}(x)|= - (1 + x)^{-2} & ⟹ & f^{″}(0)|= - (1 + 0)^{-2} =-1 \\\\ f^{(3)}(x)|= 2(1 + x)^{-3} & ⟹ & f^{‴}(0)|= 2(1 + 0)^{-3} = 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0)$, $f'(0)$, $f''(0)$, and $f'''(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_{3}(x) &= 0 + (1)(x - 0) + \\frac{1}{2!}(-1)(x - 0)^{2} + \\frac{1}{3!}(2)(x - 0)^{3} \\\\\n&= x - \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{x^{3}}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100692 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc0250e-2aa9-5439-b567-93a59fa1c364" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient of a Term In the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial of a Given Function"}] :question/id #uuid "33ce1593-08bc-539a-a7e0-c2805361d26e" :question/math-academy-id "e-742" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = e^{-2x}$?" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3!}f^{(3)}(1)\n$$\n\nLet's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= e^{-2x} \\\\\nf^{′}(x) &= -2e^{-2x} \\\\\nf^{″}(x) &= 4e^{-2x} \\\\\nf^{(3)}(x) &= -8e^{-2x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3!}f^{(3)}(1) =\\dfrac{1}{6} \\left(-8e^{-2} \\right) = -\\dfrac{4}{3e^2}\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ is\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{4}{3e^2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20824866-0419-512a-b241-e3eb66b30194" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Function Given Some Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84caa4ca-c232-5208-be43-a92090431d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x + 4) - 2(x + 4)^{2} + 2(x + 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099901} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf892fa-5884-52d9-8c6f-ec9c4e1e0d7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x - 4) - 2(x - 4)^{2} + 12(x - 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099902} {:answer/id #uuid "c18da08c-7de5-5ede-8888-76eb1b1ca737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x - 4) - (x - 4)^{2} + 2(x - 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099903} {:answer/id #uuid "07ea8d3e-c124-5a45-ad14-b59ed2aaea94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x - 4) - (x - 4)^{2} + (x - 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099904} {:answer/id #uuid "75930186-551a-54f6-8919-da2afb95a78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x + 4) - 2(x + 4)^{2} + 12(x + 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c18da08c-7de5-5ede-8888-76eb1b1ca737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x - 4) - (x - 4)^{2} + 2(x - 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099903} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee633f70-d71c-56c8-825f-ae5bc5715654" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099900}] :question/id #uuid "31b1226d-bfa8-57f5-ba65-3595a00fc98e" :question/math-academy-id "q-51235" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(4) = 1, f^{′}(4) =-1, f^{″}(4) =-2$ and $f^{‴}(4) = 12$. Which of the following is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x = 4$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "888d7cbc-e2db-59c1-8d16-b1568c832abd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{x^{2}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100483} {:answer/id #uuid "9b450de5-1314-5274-b975-e195ecb14b0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - \\frac{x^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100484} {:answer/id #uuid "b014d86e-ede1-598d-82cb-98e848515496" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\frac{x^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100485} {:answer/id #uuid "f430c847-3839-51f2-8ece-ec3c1ed29601" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - \\frac{x^{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100486} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc38953-96f7-537f-9e70-0197b8c20cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - \\frac{x^{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bc38953-96f7-537f-9e70-0197b8c20cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - \\frac{x^{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100487} :answer-field/id #uuid "53ccc27f-ba9d-5e43-b1ed-45dac3c21308" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100482}] :question/id #uuid "d8f61845-11b0-5b64-999b-d01e6c3e7c27" :question/math-academy-id "q-9360" :question/problem "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = \\sin x$ about $x = 0$ is"}]}
